WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.160
Let's look at how we adapt these skills for a child.

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:05.360
Just like with adults, you only jump in

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.800
if you see signs of severe obstruction,

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:11.900
meaning the child cannot speak, cry, or cough effectively.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.340
If they are coughing loudly, stay close

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:17.760
and encourage them to keep at it until the object comes out.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.959
When a child is choking, the most important first step

00:00:20.959 --> 00:00:22.799
is to get down to their level.

00:00:22.799 --> 00:00:26.340
Kneel or sit so your eyes are level with theirs.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:28.520
Not only does this keep them calm,

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:31.059
but it ensures you are striking and pulling

00:00:31.059 --> 00:00:33.180
at the correct angles.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:36.380
If you are standing, place one foot between theirs

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:38.220
to keep yourself steady.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.779
Alternate between the two main actions,

00:00:40.779 --> 00:00:44.220
five back blows and five abdominal thrusts.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:47.340
Keep repeating this cycle of five blows and five thrusts

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:48.820
until the object is ejected

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.779
or the child becomes unresponsive.

